@@ -9,6 +9,29 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Agent tools
+
+The sign-in and sign-up forms expose WebMCP declarative tools in supporting
+browsers after React hydrates:
+
+| Tool | Page | Required parameters |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `sign-in` | `/devtools-times/signin` | `username`, `password` |
+| `sign-up` | `/devtools-times/signup` | `username`, `password` (at least 8 characters and a number) |
+
+The browser derives the tool schemas from the named, required form inputs and
+their `toolparamdescription` attributes. Both tools use the same submission
+logic as the visible forms and return a JSON string with `{ ok, message }` after
+the API request completes. Passwords and API tokens are never included in the
+tool result. Sign-up creates an account; sign-in remains a separate operation.
+
+The forms omit `toolautosubmit`, so the browser retains its user review step
+before submitting account credentials. Browsers without WebMCP ignore the tool
+attributes and continue to use the normal forms.
+
+Run `pnpm test` with Node.js 24 or newer for automated submission and agent
+response checks; run `pnpm build` to check the production build.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
